    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "Parts a to c are routine exact values, with a negative angle converted to a coterminal one. The hardest demand is part d, where the student must generalise from three paired examples to the odd/even identities sin(-θ) = -sin θ, cos(-θ) = cos θ and tan(-θ) = -tan θ. This is a modest pattern-spotting and representation step, and the examples provide the scaffolding. Part e then applies the result to simplify an expression. This is above straight recall of exact values but well below non-trivial reframing.",
